    "draft": false,
    "pull_request": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/golang/go/pulls/81769",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/golang/go/pull/81769",
      "diff_url": "https://github.com/golang/go/pull/81769.diff",
      "patch_url": "https://github.com/golang/go/pull/81769.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "Concurrent requests currently start independent dials even when the\r\ntransport expects HTTP/2. In particular, the Go 1.27 x/net/http2 wrapper\r\nlost the dial coalescing provided by the legacy implementation.\r\n\r\nShare pending dials for HTTP/2-only transports and for x/net/http2 calls\r\nidentified by an optional UsesDialFromContext method. Publish each\r\nshared connection to the pool once and account for it once against\r\nMaxConnsPerHost. Keep ordinary HTTP/1-capable transport dials parallel,\r\nand do not share connections that fall back to HTTP/1.\r\n\r\nPreserve independent request cancellation and allow CloseIdleConnections\r\nto cancel a shared dial only when no request still needs it, including\r\nrequests queued by MaxConnsPerHost. A saturated HTTP/2 connection can\r\nstill cause another dial.\r\n\r\nAdd deterministic tests for TLS and unencrypted startup, shared dial\r\nerrors, cancellation, host isolation, connection limits, HTTP/1 fallback,\r\nand HTTP/2 stream limits.\r\n\r\nThe companion x/net change supplies the optional context method. Older\r\nx/net versions remain compatible, but require that companion change to\r\nrestore coalescing for their wrapper's default transport configuration.\r\nThe adapter and its tests are available in the companion draft PR:\r\nhttps://github.com/golang/net/pull/267\r\n\r\nA local TLS HTTP/2 reproducer with 100 simultaneous requests makes 100\r\ndials on the original transport, 1 with http2legacy, and 1 with both\r\nchanges applied, with no failed requests in any case.\r\n\r\nValidated on darwin/arm64 with go test -race net/http/...; 100\r\nrace-enabled runs of TestTransportPool; and an HTTP/1 smoke test with\r\nnethttpomithttp2. The companion x/net HTTP/2 suite passes, including its\r\nlegacy suite and 100 race-enabled runs of the new API regression tests.\r\nThe full Go all.bash suite and other platforms have not been tested.\r\n\r\nUpdates #81646",
