    "body": "### Proposal Details\n\nLinux has introduced yet another operation that can require tweaking in between fork and exec: core scheduling. Full docs are at https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/hw-vuln/core-scheduling.html. Relevant for Go is the equivalent to \"coresched new COMMAND\" or \"coresched copy -s PID COMMAND\" (see https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/coresched.1.html).\n\nI propose adding the following to `syscall.SysProcAttr`:\n\n```Go\n    // CoreSchedNew, if true, sets a new core scheduling cookie for the child. \n    CoreSchedNew bool\n    // CoreSchedPID, if not zero, sets the child's core scheduling cookie to that of PID.\n    // If the PID does not exist, the operation will fail.\n    // It is an error to set both CoreSchedNew and CoreSchedPID.\n    CoreSchedPID int\n```",
    "closed_by": null,
